{"id": "sdqa0048", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.22, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1815, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": "Asian giant hornet", "query": "What's the biggest wasp?", "transcript": "What's the biggest wasp?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The biggest wasp in the world is the Asian giant hornet, also known as the \"murder hornet.\" These insects can grow up to 1.5 inches long, with queens being larger than workers. They are found primarily in parts of Russia, Japan, and the Pacific Northwest of the United States. Their large size and powerful venom make them one of the most formidable wasps on Earth.", "answer_ms": 2491}
