{"id": "sdqa0081", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.75, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2017, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": "prepared from the plant Lawsonia inermis", "query": "How is henna made?", "transcript": "How is henna made?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Henna is made from the leaves of the Lawsonia inermis tree. The leaves are dried and ground into a fine powder. To make henna paste, the powder is mixed with water or lemon juice to create a thick paste. The mixture is then left to sit for several hours or overnight to allow the color to develop. When applied to the skin, it stains hair and skin a reddish-brown color.", "answer_ms": 2491}
