{"id": "sdqa0108", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.39, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4337, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "1955", "query": "When was Tylenol introduced?", "transcript": "When was Tylenol introduced?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time, a small dragon lived in a quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning the dragon would stretch its tiny wings and breathe warm puffs of steam into the cool air. The villagers nearby loved the dragon, bringing it gifts of honey and shiny pebbles. But one day, a storm rolled in, bringing heavy rain and strong winds. The river began to rise, threatening to flood the valley. The dragon, with all its might, breathed great plumes of fire into the clouds, trying to clear the storm. After hours of battling the tempest, the rain finally stopped. The sun broke through, shining brightly on the wet earth. The dragon, exhausted but triumphant, curled up by the now calm riverbank, dreaming of sunny days ahead.", "answer_ms": 5567}
