{"id": "sdqa0126", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.49, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1939, "eot_read_ms": 31, "reference_answer": "the process of encoding a message or information in such a way that only authorized parties can access it and those who are not authorized cannot", "query": "What is encryption?", "transcript": "What is encryption?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Encryption is a way of turning information into a secret code so that only people who have the right \"key\" can read it. Imagine you write a letter and want to send it to a friend, but you don’t want anyone else to see what’s inside. So, you scramble the words using a special method—like shifting letters or mixing them up in a pattern. Only your friend knows the secret way to unscramble it and read the message. This helps keep things like passwords, messages, or files safe from others who might try to peek!", "answer_ms": 3938}
